# Added by cargo

/target

# Library crate: consumers resolve their own lockfile.
/Cargo.lock

# Downloaded corpus sources and generated pipeline output — regenerated by
# tools/build-fragment-corpus/fetch.sh, never committed (multi-hundred-MB
# raw downloads; licensing of the generated artifact itself is still
# unresolved, see tools/build-fragment-corpus/README.md).
tools/build-fragment-corpus/data/
tools/build-fragment-corpus/target/

# Synthesizability benchmark: downloaded/preprocessed datasets and any
# generated output that reproduces raw SMILES are never committed —
# regenerated by benchmarks/synthesizability/scripts/download_brsascore.py
# and the run_*.py scripts; see benchmarks/synthesizability/datasets/README.md
# for licensing/provenance. Aggregate result files with no raw SMILES
# (benchmark_summary.json, selective_prediction.csv, timing.json) ARE
# committed, as evidence, not regenerated silently.
benchmarks/synthesizability/datasets/downloaded/
benchmarks/synthesizability/results/raw/
benchmarks/synthesizability/results/per_molecule.jsonl

# Final holdout (round 22 part 20): same policy -- raw PaRoutes files and
# any derived file carrying per-molecule SMILES are regenerable from the
# checksums/scripts in HOLDOUT_MANIFEST.md, not committed. Aggregate
# stats (leakage_audit.json, strata_and_threshold.json) and the manifest
# itself ARE committed, as the pre-registration record.
benchmarks/synthesizability/final_holdout/downloaded/
benchmarks/synthesizability/final_holdout/results/*.csv
benchmarks/synthesizability/final_holdout/results/*.jsonl

# Chemical-space error atlas (development tooling, round 22 part 12):
# per-molecule feature/embedding tables are large and fully regeneratable
# from a fixed seed (see chemical_space/README.md) -- not committed. The
# small aggregate outputs (error_regions.csv, neighbor_pairs.csv,
# summary.json) and plots ARE committed, as evidence.
benchmarks/synthesizability/chemical_space/results/features.csv
benchmarks/synthesizability/chemical_space/results/pca_coordinates.csv
benchmarks/synthesizability/chemical_space/results/umap_coordinates.csv
benchmarks/synthesizability/chemical_space/results/knn_local_rates_umap.csv

# Information-loss audit (development tooling, round 22 part 13):
# per-molecule feature tables are large and fully regeneratable from a
# fixed seed (see information_loss_audit/README.md) -- not committed.
# The small aggregate outputs (probe_results.json, add_drop_results.json,
# fn_archetypes.json, fold_summary.json, stereo_contradiction_*) ARE
# committed, as evidence.
benchmarks/synthesizability/information_loss_audit/results/features.csv
benchmarks/synthesizability/information_loss_audit/results/features_with_folds.csv

